# 04 - Project Charter

## 1. Project Title

Student Planner and Management System

## 2. Project Purpose

Develop a simple system that helps students organize class schedules, study plans, assignments, projects, and exam dates.

## 3. Project Objectives

- Provide a weekly class timetable.
- Allow students to create study plans.
- Store assignments and projects with due dates.
- Record exam dates.
- Show task status as completed or pending.
- Display upcoming academic activities.

## 4. Project Scope

### In Scope

- Adding, editing, and deleting class schedule entries.
- Creating and managing study sessions.
- Recording assignments and projects.
- Recording exam dates.
- Tracking completed and pending tasks.
- Viewing upcoming activities.

### Out of Scope

- Online payment.
- Communication with university databases.
- Automatic synchronization with university systems.
- Advanced AI study recommendations.
- Multi-user social features.

## 5. Main Deliverables

1. Project README file.
2. Client Request document.
3. System Request document.
4. Feasibility Analysis document.
5. Project Charter document.
6. A basic working version of the Student Planner system in the development phase.

## 6. Main Stakeholders

- Primary user: Student.
- Project developer: Student/development team.
- Course instructor: Reviews the project and its documentation.

## 7. Estimated Schedule

| Phase | Main Activities | Estimated Duration |
|---|---|---|
| Planning | Define needs and prepare planning documents | 1 week |
| Analysis and Design | Identify requirements and design screens/database | 1 week |
| Development | Implement core features | 3 weeks |
| Testing | Test features and correct errors | 1 week |
| Final Review | Prepare final project and documentation | 1 week |

## 8. Main Risks

- Limited time for development.
- Errors in entering or saving information.
- Changes to requirements during development.
- Loss of stored data.

## 9. Success Criteria

The project will be considered successful if students can:

- Enter and view their class timetable.
- Create study plans.
- Record assignments and exam dates.
- Identify completed and pending tasks.
- Use the main features without difficulty.

## 10. Approval

This charter defines the initial plan and scope of the Student Planner and Management System. Any major change to the scope should be reviewed before implementation.
